Bind FORTE's TCP server sockets to the address they were given.

At efcd63c, openTCPServerConnection ignores its address and binds INADDR_ANY, so `forte -c 127.0.0.1:61499`
still exposes the unauthenticated management port (DEV_MGR) on every interface. test_stack.py found this.
Any peer on the OT network could then rewrite the running application, including the fencing token.
With this patch the management port is reachable from inside the container only.

--- a/core/arch/common/src/bsdsocketinterf.cpp
+++ b/core/arch/common/src/bsdsocketinterf.cpp
@@ -62,7 +62,10 @@
 #else
     stSockAddr.sin_port = htons(paPort);
 #endif
-    stSockAddr.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl(INADDR_ANY);
+    stSockAddr.sin_addr.s_addr = inet_addr(paIPAddr);
+    if (stSockAddr.sin_addr.s_addr == INADDR_NONE) {
+      stSockAddr.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl(INADDR_ANY); // A host name such as "localhost": keep the old behaviour.
+    }
 
     if (bind(nSocket, (struct sockaddr *) &stSockAddr, sizeof(struct sockaddr)) != 0) {
       DEVLOG_ERROR("CBSDSocketInterface: bind() failed: %s\n", strerror(errno));
